            </note>
            <note corresp="#d304-f2" n="2" xml:id="d304-f2-content">
                <p>Reference is to Bulganin’s message of September 19. See <ref target="#d304-f4"
                        >footnote 4, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d304-f3" n="3" xml:id="d304-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d300">Document 300</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d304-f4" n="4" xml:id="d304-f4-content">
                <p>According to Secretary Dulles’ Appointment Book,Dulles had dinner with the
                    Merchants at their home at 8 p.m. (Princeton University Library, Dulles
                    Papers)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d304-f5" n="5" xml:id="d304-f5-content">
                <p>According to Dulles’ Appointment Book, the Secretary met at 8:30 a.m., September
                    24, with Jernegan,Merchant,Phleger, and Allen to discuss the Soviets’ sale of
                    arms to Egypt. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid</hi>.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
